WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.303 line:0%
DR. T: Oh, look at those
beautiful teeth you have.

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.038 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR:
 Deep in the heart of Texas,</i>

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:09.909 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
<i> there's no such thing as
 a typical patient for Dr. T,</i>

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.379 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
<i> and that includes Shiloh,
 a four-year-old scarlet macaw</i>

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.281 line:0%
<i> with an itchy predicament.</i>

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.482 line:0%
REBECCA: Shiloh got her name

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:19.586 line:0%
because I am a big
Neil Diamond fan.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:23.789
And there's a song by that name,
Shiloh, and she is my companion.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.157
She goes with me places,

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
we go to elementary schools,
we go to nursing homes.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.330
She loves that, you know,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the people really enjoy
getting to see her.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.633
<i> NARRATOR: But lately,
 Shiloh isn't acting</i>

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:37.737
<i> like her usual, happy self.</i>

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.340
REBECCA: She just spends most of
her time pulling at her feathers

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.341 align:start position:0%
or preening her feathers,
which she's doing with her beak,

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:43.910
and she's damaging them.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.578 align:start size:81% position:19%
There must be
an underlying issue

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's why I brought her
here today.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:50.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. T: Hi. I'm Dr. Thielen,
nice to meet you.

00:00:50.482 --> 00:00:53.653
Hey, pretty girl.
You are gorgeous.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.087
So, tell me exactly
where she's picking,

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:56.789
and can you even
show me with her,

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.124
I don't have to touch her yet.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.526 align:start position:0%
REBECCA: This is where
she's been picking, looks like.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:03.162
Right at the base of where
her tail meets the body.

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. T: That's the only spot,
though?

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.765
Oh, okay.

00:01:06.765 --> 00:01:09.535 align:start size:97% position:3%
REBECCA: What she's aiming at,
what she's trying to get...

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:10.536
DR. T: Is the feather shaft.

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.504 align:start size:81% position:19%
REBECCA: Yes.
And they're bloody.

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:13.907
And that's what's worrying me.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.407
DR. T: I agree.

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:18.678 align:start position:0%
Preening is the behavior that
a bird does to groom themselves.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.347 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
In Shiloh's case,
she's taking it to the extreme

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
and we need to figure out
why that is.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.917
How often does she bathe?

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.385
REBECCA: That's the other thing.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:29.255
She won't come near me for days
if I take her to the shower.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.723
DR. T: Oh.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.092 align:start position:0%
REBECCA: And I've actually taken
her and put her on my chest

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.296 align:start position:0%
with a T-shirt on in the shower,
and she just gets that,

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:88% position:13%
she's just quaking
and does that "uhrrrr."

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:42.134
DR. T: If Shiloh's not bathing,
it can be a serious problem,

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:44.870 align:start size:91% position:9%
because, in parrots,
baths are pretty necessary

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start position:0%
in order to keep their skin
and feathers clean and healthy.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.609
Otherwise, dirt and dander can
build up and trigger anything

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:53.813 align:start size:84% position:16%
from abnormal preening
to even infections.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.481
She is preening a lot.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.083
REBECCA: Oh, yeah,
it's just constant.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.084 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. T: Does she do that
at home this much?

00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:00.487 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, my bird preens,
but jeez,

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.355 align:start size:91% position:9%
I mean, she hasn't stopped
since we've been here.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.656
REBECCA: No, uh-uh.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.525
But she'll just sit there
and do that for hours.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.360
I try to divert her attention,
I get, you know, nuts for her,

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.497 align:start position:0%
she loves pine nuts, and I'll
give her three or four of those.

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:14.867 align:start position:0%
DR. T: Yeah, she's like obsessed
with it, is what's happening.

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.068
Not even just her tail,

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:17.503 align:start size:88% position:13%
that's what she's doing
the most damage to,

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:18.804
but just preening in general.

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:20.306
She just seems very agitated.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.407
REBECCA: She is.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.542
DR. T: Is she going
to let me hold her?

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:24.977
REBECCA: Well, she may.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.079
DR. T: I'll just see.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.314 align:start size:84% position:16%
Hi, pretty girl.
You gonna go onto me?

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.349
Want to come up? Good girl!

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.151
What a good bird, sweetheart.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:34.320
Your momma's right here.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you just beautiful?
Look at your orange cheeks.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.892 align:start size:78% position:22%
Your orange cheeks
are so pretty.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:42.061
Can I pet you? Yeah?

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.163
Oh, oh, oh. Yes, you're
a good girl, aren't you?

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:47.867 align:start position:0%
Seeing Shiloh this uncomfortable
and in obvious distress

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:52.038
is painful for me, so I can only
imagine what Shiloh feels like.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:55.207 align:start position:0%
I'm a bird mom, too,
and I know if this was my bird,

00:02:55.207 --> 00:02:58.177 align:start position:0%
I'd do whatever it takes to make
her happy and healthy again.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:01.413 align:start position:0%
So I'm definitely going do
everything I can to help Shiloh.

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:02.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
These feathers
don't look healthy, though.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.316
Do you see them,
how they're black?

00:03:04.316 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:91% position:9%
And they just look brittle
and not normal.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.324
REBECCA: Because of
the not bathing?

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:13.159
DR. T: Maybe.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.294
Parrots in general are
these highly intelligent,

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:17.430
extremely social beings

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.533 align:start size:97% position:3%
who can have a lot of problems
in captivity.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:24.203
Oftentimes there's some
kind of anxiety going on

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:27.339
that causes them to over-preen.

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:29.642
Because those feathers
just don't look normal,

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.177
I'm actually thinking that
her preening all the time

00:03:32.177 --> 00:03:33.512
isn't psychogenic,

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:36.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
there actually may be
an underlying medical cause.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.950
I definitely want to do
a basic medical work-up,

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.887
but I do have some things in
mind that I want to test for,

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:44.290
that would mainly involve
her skin and feathers.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.391 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: For Shiloh's safety
 and comfort,</i>

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:47.960
<i> Dr. T gives her a sedative.</i>

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.028
(squawk)

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.496 align:start size:88% position:13%
MARYANNE: In the muscle.
TONYA: Go sleepy.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.064 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Takes a blood sample.</i>
 MARYANNE: There you go.

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:53.065
<i> NARRATOR: A feather.</i>

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:55.001
DR. T: One, two.
(Maryanne gasps)

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.903
I'm sorry, I'm sorry,
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: And a slide
 impression of Shiloh's skin</i>

00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:00.639
<i> will be submitted for testing.</i>

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:01.974 align:start size:81% position:19%
DR. T: Now it's just
a waiting game.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:03.475
We are sending everything off

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:06.546
and we're just gonna wait
on results to make a plan.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.919 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Just down the hall
 is Tex Rex,</i>

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:17.323 line:0%
<i> a four-year-old bearded dragon
 with an appetite for disaster.</i>

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Thankfully, Dr. Bruce Nixon
 is here to help.</i>

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.261 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. NIXON: Hi, I'm Dr. Nixon,
how are you doing?

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:23.663 align:start size:81% position:19%
KELLI: Hi. Hi, good,
how are you?

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:25.464 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. NIXON: So, I hear that
you have a dragon

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:27.733
who thinks he's a coin purse?

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:28.835
KELLI: Yes.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.636
While I was out to dinner,

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:34.807 line:0%
I get a hysterical call
from my 13-year-old son.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:38.110 align:start size:97% position:3%
He walked in his room and
he threw his wallet on the bed

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.512
and a couple of coins fell out.

00:04:40.512 --> 00:04:42.581 align:start size:97% position:3%
Rex is walking around,
and he goes, all of a sudden,

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:46.018
he just saw that penny and
he went over and ate it,

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:49.321
before he could do
anything about it.

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:52.024
DR. NIXON: Hello, Rex.

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:53.259
I know.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:55.127 align:start size:81% position:19%
Pennies are actually
made of zinc,

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:59.498 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and zinc causes
a heavy metal toxicosis, okay?

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:02.435 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
And this can really
make them ill.

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:05.371 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Heavy metal toxicosis
 can damage internal organs,</i>

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:08.875
<i> trigger anemia and
 even cause death.</i>

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.509
<i> There's no time to wait.</i>

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:12.278
<i> The penny must come out now.</i>

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.779 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. NIXON: We're gonna do this
step by step.

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:18.684
First of all, we want to make
sure that it's really in there.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:20.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's easy, we're gonna get
an x-ray taken.

00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:21.721 align:start size:75% position:25%
KELLI: Okay.
DR. NIXON: Okay?

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.389 align:start size:81% position:19%
DR. NIXON: Then what
we're going to do

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:26.358 align:start size:88% position:13%
is we're going to
anesthetize him briefly

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:28.427
and what we're probably gonna do

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:32.231 align:start size:88% position:13%
is use what's called
a rigid endoscope, okay,

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:34.934
to actually go in
under anesthesia,

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.869 align:start size:81% position:19%
through the mouth
and into the stomach

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:41.040 align:start position:0%
and we can probably get this out
without doing surgery.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.375
KELLI: That was our hope,

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:46.111
that hopefully it could be
removed without surgery.

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:47.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. NIXON: If you'll let me
borrow him for a minute

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:49.548
and we'll take a quick x-ray

00:05:49.548 --> 00:05:52.484 align:start size:91% position:9%
and we'll make sure
that it's in there, okay?

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:53.986
KELLI: Okay.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:58.724 align:start size:97% position:3%
My son loves this dragon so
much, Tex Rex, he's his buddy.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:01.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's been texting me all day
from school.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.630
He is beside himself with worry

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:08.333 align:start size:81% position:19%
and I think he feels
very responsible.

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:09.535 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. NIXON:
Get a radiograph on him.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:10.903
JACOB: No problem.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:13.673
KELLI: And I know my son
would be very, very worried

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:16.576
if he had to have surgery.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.480
JACOB: Oh, there it is.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.850 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Tex Rex's x-ray
 results are beyond conclusive.</i>

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:26.986
DR. NIXON: No, there's the
Lincoln Memorial right there.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:29.322 align:start position:0%
We've definitely got it in here,
so what we need to do now

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:34.393
is to prepare for some
endoscopic retrieval.

00:06:34.393 --> 00:06:38.263 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Dr. Nixon drafts
 Dr. T to be his right-hand vet.</i>

00:06:38.263 --> 00:06:39.565
DR. NIXON: We're gonna do good.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.335
DR. T: Yay! I'm so excited.

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:45.237 align:start position:0%
As a vet, there's no such thing
as knowing too much,

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:47.607 align:start size:88% position:13%
and one of the things
I love most about my job

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.342 align:start size:78% position:22%
is that I'm always
learning more.

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:52.544
And I get to collaborate with
other amazingly talented vets,

00:06:52.544 --> 00:06:56.615
like Dr. Nixon, who has a ton
of knowledge and experience.

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:58.584 align:start size:84% position:16%
So not only does that
benefit me,

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.953 align:start size:78% position:22%
it benefits all
our patients, too.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.422
DR. NIXON: Open.

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:04.323 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: As soon as
 the anesthesia kicks in,</i>

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:08.861
<i> it's time for Dr. Nixon
 and Dr. T to get to work.</i>

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:09.995
DR. T: Okay.

00:07:09.995 --> 00:07:11.696 align:start size:88% position:13%
We're choosing endoscopy
instead of a surgery

00:07:11.696 --> 00:07:14.500
because it's much less invasive,

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.936 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's no surgery that
the animal needs to heal from,

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:19.372
and if the penny
went in that way,

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:22.008 align:start size:91% position:9%
it means it should be able
to come out that way.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:24.843
Going down the esophagus.

00:07:24.843 --> 00:07:26.111
DR. NIXON: Esophagus.

00:07:26.111 --> 00:07:28.547
We're going to go
into the stomach

00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:32.017 align:start size:84% position:16%
and actually visually
see that penny,

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:33.618
and this is where
Dr. Thielen and I

00:07:33.618 --> 00:07:35.387
are gonna be working in concert.

00:07:35.387 --> 00:07:37.789
So she's going to
locate the penny

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:39.524
and she's gonna hold it steady,

00:07:39.524 --> 00:07:41.726 align:start size:91% position:9%
and then I'm gonna come in
right behind her

00:07:41.726 --> 00:07:43.395
and I'm gonna grab the penny,

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:45.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
which means that I will get
all of the glory.

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:48.367 align:start size:81% position:19%
So, this should work
marvelously.

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:52.337 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Next door, Molly,</i>

00:07:52.337 --> 00:07:54.873 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
<i> a newly adopted
 Flemish giant rabbit,</i>

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:58.811 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i> lands in the ER,
 and she's in dire straits.</i>

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:01.613 line:0%
MAIKE: We've only had her
at home for three days.

00:08:01.613 --> 00:08:04.149 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
The person at the rescue
said that the owners

00:08:04.149 --> 00:08:06.318 line:0%
could no longer afford her care.

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:09.721 align:start position:0% line:0%
DEREK: So, we flew to California
and then we brought her back.

00:08:09.721 --> 00:08:11.590
MAIKE: She was just
recently spayed,

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.558 align:start size:91% position:9%
but other than that,
she seemed in good shape.

00:08:13.558 --> 00:08:16.995 align:start size:84% position:16%
But then we noticed
that she was bleeding,

00:08:16.995 --> 00:08:20.332 align:start size:97% position:3%
and so we checked her belly
and we saw that some big thing

00:08:20.332 --> 00:08:22.535
was sticking out
of her incision.

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:27.473 align:start position:0%
MAIKE: And so we just rushed her
here as soon as we noticed,

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:30.075 align:start size:97% position:3%
because we were scared she was
gonna die on the drive.

00:08:30.075 --> 00:08:30.977
DR. FREEMAN: Oh, jeez.

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.313 align:start position:0%
DR. FREEMAN: She actually
started chewing on her incision,

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:38.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
so her urinary bladder is
sticking out of her abdomen.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.453 line:0%
We need to figure out a way to
put it back in and stabilize her

00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:44.089
until Dr. Thielen can see her.

00:08:44.089 --> 00:08:46.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Molly's condition
 is so serious,</i>

00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:50.428
<i> even the ER hospital's Chief
 of Medicine steps in to help.</i>

00:08:50.428 --> 00:08:51.764 line:0%
DR. TURNER: This is shocking.

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:54.466 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
We don't typically see
animals come in

00:08:54.466 --> 00:08:56.936 line:0%
with their bladders
outside their body.

00:08:58.837 --> 00:09:00.506 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. TURNER:
That makes me a little worried
that might be the ureter.

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:03.275 align:start size:88% position:13%
One of her ureters
is bruised and inflamed

00:09:03.275 --> 00:09:05.010
and possibly damaged.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.845
DR. FREEMAN: So there's a little
bit of ulcerations right here.

00:09:06.845 --> 00:09:08.514 align:start size:81% position:19%
DR. TURNER: This is
a huge problem,

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:12.918 align:start size:97% position:3%
because the ureter is what
allows urine to be transported

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:14.720
from the kidney to the bladder,

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.056 align:start size:97% position:3%
and a damaged ureter can lead
to kidney failure,

00:09:18.056 --> 00:09:20.593 align:start size:88% position:13%
as well as a number
of other complications.

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:22.294
Let's get this cleaned up,

00:09:22.294 --> 00:09:25.531
get that bladder back in
as quickly as possible,

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:28.467 align:start position:0%
'cause we don't want impingement
on that second ureter.

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:30.369
DR. FREEMAN: Yeah, okay.

00:09:39.311 --> 00:09:40.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. TURNER: Molly's bladder
is so inflamed

00:09:40.879 --> 00:09:43.916 align:start size:97% position:3%
that it is not fitting back
through her tiny spay incision

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:45.451
that had opened up.

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:46.551 align:start size:88% position:13%
The bladder's not going
back in the hole.

00:09:46.551 --> 00:09:47.753
DR. FREEMAN: Yeah.

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:48.754
DR. TURNER: Which was
sort of the easy way.

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:50.122
DR. FREEMAN: Yeah.

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:51.223 align:start position:0%
DR. TURNER: So at the very least
we're gonna have to extend

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:53.225
that incision, flush the belly,

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:56.295 align:start position:0%
we're worried about the ureter,
the kidney may have to go.

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:58.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
We are gonna need to get her
into the surgery suite

00:09:58.763 --> 00:10:00.833
so we can extend this incision,

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:03.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
get a better look at what
possible damage has occurred

00:10:03.135 --> 00:10:08.073 align:start position:0%
in her body and get this bladder
back in as soon as we can.

00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:09.575
<i> NARRATOR: Molly is
 given anesthesia</i>

00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:11.510
<i> and prepped for surgery.</i>

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:18.985 align:start size:91% position:9%
HAYLEY: Hey, we need
for a doctor in here now!

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:24.856
Freeman, it's your bunny on CPR.

00:10:24.856 --> 00:10:27.692
DR. TURNER: What is the issue?

00:10:27.692 --> 00:10:29.261
What is the issue?

00:10:29.261 --> 00:10:30.595
HAYLEY: Stopped breathing.

00:10:30.595 --> 00:10:31.430
DR. TURNER: Okay.

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:41.006 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Molly, the Flemish
 giant rabbit's bladder</i>

00:10:41.006 --> 00:10:43.208 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
<i> is completely outside
 of her body,</i>

00:10:43.208 --> 00:10:46.478 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i> and she needs emergency surgery
 to get it back in.</i>

00:10:46.478 --> 00:10:48.681
<i> But before surgery even begins,</i>

00:10:48.681 --> 00:10:52.284
<i> her condition takes
 a critical nosedive.</i>

00:10:52.284 --> 00:10:55.287
DR. TURNER: Go ahead and
give this half IV, half IM.

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:56.454
We don't usually give it IV,

00:10:56.454 --> 00:10:58.357
but we're going to have
to make an exception.

00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:02.594 align:start position:0% line:0%
Molly has flat-lined on us after
we gave her the medications

00:11:02.594 --> 00:11:04.195 line:0%
to induce anesthesia.

00:11:04.195 --> 00:11:07.599 line:0%
We are working quickly
to try and get her back.

00:11:07.599 --> 00:11:09.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
We lost heart and the rabbit
stopped breathing

00:11:09.969 --> 00:11:11.703
and we did get
a heartbeat back.

00:11:11.703 --> 00:11:13.972 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Have we taken any spontaneous
breaths at this point?

00:11:13.972 --> 00:11:15.440 line:0%
Okay.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:18.944
These owners literally just got
this rabbit within the week.

00:11:18.944 --> 00:11:21.212
They went all the way to
California for this bunny,

00:11:21.212 --> 00:11:23.449
so this is a big deal to them,

00:11:23.449 --> 00:11:26.719
and even in the short period of
time, we've all gotten attached,

00:11:26.719 --> 00:11:29.021
so it's a big deal to us.

00:11:34.326 --> 00:11:36.462 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. TURNER: Thankfully,
Molly has responded

00:11:36.462 --> 00:11:39.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is more stable,
so we need to get in there,

00:11:39.464 --> 00:11:43.235
get that bladder back in and
get her sewed up right now.

00:11:43.235 --> 00:11:44.503
<i> NARRATOR: But within minutes,</i>

00:11:44.503 --> 00:11:46.972 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> Molly's heart rate
 plunges again.</i>

00:11:46.972 --> 00:11:48.708 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. TURNER: Do you have
femoral pulse?

00:12:00.786 --> 00:12:02.687 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. TURNER: Molly's heart rate
has dropped on us again.

00:12:02.687 --> 00:12:06.158
I am really worried she's going
to arrest on us a second time,

00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:07.926
but Molly is not
going to survive

00:12:07.926 --> 00:12:09.861 align:start size:91% position:9%
unless we get this bladder
back in,

00:12:09.861 --> 00:12:13.198 align:start position:0%
so we are going to move forward
as quickly as possible,

00:12:13.198 --> 00:12:15.768 align:start size:88% position:13%
open that incision,
get the bladder back in,

00:12:15.768 --> 00:12:20.306 align:start position:0%
and then hopefully get her more
stable to see Dr. Thielen.

00:12:26.178 --> 00:12:27.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
How much has her heart rate
slowed down, anybody?

00:12:27.613 --> 00:12:28.947
TONYA: Quite a bit.

00:12:28.947 --> 00:12:30.583
DR. TURNER: What number?
Did she have a heartbeat?

00:12:30.583 --> 00:12:33.185 align:start size:81% position:19%
TONYA: Yes, she has
a heartbeat.

00:12:33.185 --> 00:12:36.421
<i> NARRATOR: Dr. Turner swiftly
 extends Molly's spay incision</i>

00:12:36.421 --> 00:12:39.325
<i> and inserts her bladder
 back inside her body.</i>

00:12:47.899 --> 00:12:51.103 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: And for now, Molly's
 close brush with death</i>

00:12:51.103 --> 00:12:53.472
<i> appears to be behind her.</i>

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:54.873 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. FREEMAN: There you go.
KIM: There you go.

00:12:54.873 --> 00:12:57.643
DR. FREEMAN: Wake up. Hi!

00:12:57.643 --> 00:12:59.611 align:start size:88% position:13%
HAYLEY: Hey, Molly.
KIM: Oh, that's better.

00:12:59.611 --> 00:13:02.047
DR. FREEMAN: Hey, Molly.

00:13:02.047 --> 00:13:04.850
HAYLEY: Hi! Yeah, hi.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:09.120
DR. TURNER: We don't always see
these guys survive to discharge,

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:13.292
but sometimes what we have to
focus in on is the teamwork

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:14.659
and the small wins,

00:13:14.659 --> 00:13:17.129 align:start size:91% position:9%
and this was a really good
example of teamwork

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:22.735
and at least a small step
in the right direction, so.

00:13:22.735 --> 00:13:24.569
Good job, everybody.

00:13:24.569 --> 00:13:26.071
DR. FREEMAN: Good job.

00:13:26.071 --> 00:13:28.640
DR. TURNER: Molly is far from
out of the woods at this point.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.043 align:start size:91% position:9%
We are going to hopefully
get her more stable

00:13:31.043 --> 00:13:34.213 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then we can transfer
the rabbit's care

00:13:34.213 --> 00:13:38.049 align:start size:91% position:9%
to Dr. Thielen's practice
completely.

00:13:38.049 --> 00:13:40.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Molly has made it
 through her surgery,</i>

00:13:40.185 --> 00:13:44.523 align:start position:0%
<i> but Tex Rex is still
 stomach-deep in his endoscopy.</i>

00:13:44.523 --> 00:13:46.725 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. T: I see that brown thing,
but that's not a penny.

00:13:46.725 --> 00:13:48.727
What is that? Food?

00:13:48.727 --> 00:13:50.329
DR. NIXON: Poke it.

00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:51.530
DR. T: It's gotta be food.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:54.165 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. NIXON: Well, unfortunately
it had a meal

00:13:54.165 --> 00:13:56.234
right before it ate the penny.

00:13:56.234 --> 00:13:58.370 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: Tex Rex has
 a potentially toxic penny</i>

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:02.273
<i> in his stomach that needs
 to come out immediately.</i>

00:14:02.273 --> 00:14:06.311
<i> But this penny is
 playing hard to get.</i>

00:14:06.311 --> 00:14:07.613
DR. T: So, I'm trying
to find this penny

00:14:07.613 --> 00:14:10.249 align:start size:81% position:19%
in this sea of
bearded dragon food,

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:14.019 align:start position:0% line:0%
and it's just, oh, my god,
this is a frustrating nightmare.

00:14:14.019 --> 00:14:16.021
DR. NIXON: The thing that
is complicating matters

00:14:16.021 --> 00:14:18.524 align:start size:84% position:16%
is all of the food
that's in the stomach.

00:14:18.524 --> 00:14:21.493 align:start size:97% position:3%
If it was just a penny,
this would be a piece of cake,

00:14:21.493 --> 00:14:25.296
but all the food is
getting in the way.

00:14:25.296 --> 00:14:27.766 align:start position:0%
DR. T: With the endoscopy, we
always have to just keep in mind

00:14:27.766 --> 00:14:30.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this camera is not only
really magnified,

00:14:30.702 --> 00:14:33.472 align:start size:91% position:9%
but every movement,
every little tiny movement

00:14:33.472 --> 00:14:35.607 align:start size:88% position:13%
is a really big movement
on the screen.

00:14:35.607 --> 00:14:36.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. NIXON: Whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:14:36.641 --> 00:14:37.776 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. T: Oh, wait,
whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:14:37.776 --> 00:14:39.845 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, although it's
pretty straightforward

00:14:39.845 --> 00:14:41.613 align:start size:91% position:9%
with how you have to move
the camera,

00:14:41.613 --> 00:14:43.682 align:start size:84% position:16%
finding the penny
through all that food

00:14:43.682 --> 00:14:45.483
is not as easy as it looks.

00:14:45.483 --> 00:14:48.553 align:start size:84% position:16%
Where'd it go?
I just saw something.

00:14:48.553 --> 00:14:50.121 align:start position:0%
DR. T: See, it is a mealworm.
DR. NIXON: Yeah, that is a worm.

00:14:50.121 --> 00:14:51.690
DR. T: Oh, that is so gross.

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:53.558 align:start size:81% position:19%
It's like a waxworm
or something.

00:14:53.558 --> 00:14:55.160
I think you're gonna
have to insufflate it.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.696
So we're gonna actually
have to do insufflation.

00:14:57.696 --> 00:14:59.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're gonna fill the stomach
with some water,

00:14:59.531 --> 00:15:00.965
so that way it distends

00:15:00.965 --> 00:15:03.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be able to swirl around
all the food,

00:15:03.101 --> 00:15:06.038 align:start position:0%
so hopefully I can see the penny
with inside the stomach.

00:15:06.038 --> 00:15:07.806 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. NIXON: It's a salad
inside right now.

00:15:07.806 --> 00:15:10.809
We're gonna make it a water
balloon with a salad inside.

00:15:10.809 --> 00:15:11.910
DR. T: Okay.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.445
When I'm doing the insufflation,

00:15:13.445 --> 00:15:15.714 align:start size:88% position:13%
the most important thing
is that Tex Rex

00:15:15.714 --> 00:15:18.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
doesn't accidentally inhale
some of this water,

00:15:18.083 --> 00:15:19.151
'cause if that happens

00:15:19.151 --> 00:15:20.920 align:start size:81% position:19%
and enough liquid
gets into his lungs,

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.388 align:start size:97% position:3%
at the very least
it's gonna cause an infection,

00:15:23.388 --> 00:15:25.424
or it could even kill him.

00:15:25.424 --> 00:15:28.326 align:start size:97% position:3%
So we're going to intubate him
to prevent any extra fluid

00:15:28.326 --> 00:15:30.128
that's overfilling
from his stomach

00:15:30.128 --> 00:15:32.164
from going down his trachea.

00:15:32.164 --> 00:15:33.164
Okay.

00:15:33.164 --> 00:15:34.266
DR. NIXON: That's much better.

00:15:34.266 --> 00:15:36.668 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. T: Yes.
Just still watch the tube.

00:15:36.668 --> 00:15:38.136
Okay, so now we go again.

00:15:38.136 --> 00:15:39.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
The whole time we still have
to keep in mind, though,

00:15:39.805 --> 00:15:42.340 align:start size:91% position:9%
that we're inside
a really sensitive organ,

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.843 align:start position:0%
so you want to be really careful
and not too rough.

00:15:44.843 --> 00:15:46.678 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. NIXON: Is that it
right there?

00:15:46.678 --> 00:15:47.912
DR. T: That's your mealworm.

00:15:47.912 --> 00:15:49.647 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. NIXON:
Oh, that is a mealworm.

00:15:49.647 --> 00:15:52.284
DR. T: That's as far as it goes.

00:15:52.284 --> 00:15:53.352
DR. NIXON: Okay.

00:15:53.352 --> 00:15:56.088
DR. T: I'm just not
seeing the penny.

00:15:56.088 --> 00:15:58.657 align:start size:81% position:19%
Everything but
the frickin' penny.

00:15:58.657 --> 00:15:59.791
DR. NIXON: No kidding.

00:15:59.791 --> 00:16:01.193
There it is!

00:16:01.193 --> 00:16:02.261
DR. T: (gasps) There it is,
there it is, there it is.

00:16:02.261 --> 00:16:04.062 align:start size:88% position:13%
Don't move, don't move,
don't move.

00:16:04.062 --> 00:16:05.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. NIXON: Instrument.
DR. T: Grabbers.

00:16:05.163 --> 00:16:06.998
DR. NIXON: Got it.

00:16:06.998 --> 00:16:10.868
Everybody just be still.

00:16:10.868 --> 00:16:12.571
DR. T: I'm gonna advance you.

00:16:12.571 --> 00:16:13.906
Open.

00:16:17.208 --> 00:16:19.511
Oh, (bleep), I can't see it.

00:16:19.511 --> 00:16:20.745
Where'd it go?

00:16:20.745 --> 00:16:22.781
Oh, no, where'd it go?

00:16:26.451 --> 00:16:27.920 line:0%
DR. T: Where'd it go?
Oh, no, where'd it go?

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.355 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: A four-year-old
 bearded dragon, Tex Rex,</i>

00:16:30.355 --> 00:16:33.058 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
<i> has a potentially toxic penny
 inside his stomach,</i>

00:16:33.058 --> 00:16:36.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> and Dr. T and Dr. Nixon are
 on a mission to find it</i>

00:16:36.261 --> 00:16:38.263
<i> and get it out.</i>

00:16:38.263 --> 00:16:41.967
<i> But a belly full of food
 is foiling their plans.</i>

00:16:41.967 --> 00:16:45.103 align:start position:0%
DR. NIXON: We can see the salad,
we can see the worms.

00:16:45.103 --> 00:16:47.138
Okay, let's do this.

00:16:47.138 --> 00:16:50.041 align:start size:84% position:16%
Take everything out
and now let's palpate.

00:16:50.041 --> 00:16:52.076 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. T: We're not having
great success

00:16:52.076 --> 00:16:54.046 line:0%
with our endoscopy exploration.

00:16:54.046 --> 00:16:56.815
So, desperate times call
for desperate measures.

00:16:56.815 --> 00:16:59.985 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're gonna have
to try something else.

00:16:59.985 --> 00:17:03.554 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Dr. Nixon physically
 locates the penny.</i>

00:17:03.554 --> 00:17:05.891 align:start position:0%
DR. NIXON: I'm holding the penny
in my fingers.

00:17:05.891 --> 00:17:07.225 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. T: You're holding
the penny in your fingers.

00:17:07.225 --> 00:17:09.294
DR. NIXON: Mm-hm, yep, I am.

00:17:09.294 --> 00:17:11.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. T: Well, hang on, then,
let me find it.

00:17:11.496 --> 00:17:14.399 align:start position:0%
I'm thinking that, since I have
a pretty good idea

00:17:14.399 --> 00:17:16.134 align:start size:84% position:16%
of where the penny is
in the stomach,

00:17:16.134 --> 00:17:19.070 align:start size:91% position:9%
if I can get an instrument
really carefully

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:20.572
down into the stomach,

00:17:20.572 --> 00:17:23.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
I might be able to feel that
metal on metal sensation,

00:17:23.708 --> 00:17:26.378 align:start size:91% position:9%
be able to find the penny
and pull it out.

00:17:26.378 --> 00:17:27.379
Ready? Ready?

00:17:27.379 --> 00:17:29.714
DR. NIXON: Yeah.

00:17:29.714 --> 00:17:32.150
DR. T: Whaaaaaa!!

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:34.152
(laughs)

00:17:34.152 --> 00:17:37.389
Oh, my god!

00:17:37.389 --> 00:17:38.657
That was insane!

00:17:38.657 --> 00:17:42.160
It's a 2002 Abe Lincoln.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.229
DR. NIXON: Superstars.

00:17:44.229 --> 00:17:46.731
DR. T: This is amazing.

00:17:46.731 --> 00:17:49.834 align:start size:88% position:13%
We were in there with
our big, fancy equipment

00:17:49.834 --> 00:17:52.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
and all you needed was
a pair of forceps

00:17:52.203 --> 00:17:55.173 align:start position:0%
and go down the bearded dragon,
and there's your penny.

00:17:55.173 --> 00:17:56.174
(laughs)

00:17:56.174 --> 00:17:57.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. NIXON: That does not
belong to us,

00:17:57.175 --> 00:17:58.710
that belongs to the client.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:02.414 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Tex Rex is now
 penny-free and free to go home.</i>

00:18:02.414 --> 00:18:03.481
DR. NIXON: Look who I have.

00:18:03.481 --> 00:18:05.116
KELLI: Aw, there he is.

00:18:05.116 --> 00:18:06.752
He's probably glad to see you.

00:18:06.752 --> 00:18:09.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. NIXON: Now you can tell
all your friends

00:18:09.187 --> 00:18:13.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
that your bearded dragon
is now penniless, he's poor.

00:18:13.925 --> 00:18:15.694 line:0%
KELLI: Here's the penny,

00:18:15.694 --> 00:18:18.963 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and it looks just like it did
on the x-ray.

00:18:18.963 --> 00:18:20.098 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. NIXON: It wasn't in there
long enough

00:18:20.098 --> 00:18:22.800
to cause any kind
of zinc toxicosis,

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:24.436
so this should be the end of it.

00:18:24.436 --> 00:18:26.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
KELLI: Ben's gonna decide
what he wants to do with it.

00:18:26.304 --> 00:18:28.140
Make jewelry or frame it.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.675
BENJAMIN: Frame it.

