If this gets gross, you can wipe
it with some dilute iodine.

00:27:17.868 --> 00:27:21.071 align:start size:97% position:3%
You just mix a couple drops
of iodine with some warm water

00:27:21.071 --> 00:27:23.407
so it looks like iced tea color.

00:27:23.407 --> 00:27:25.944 align:start size:97% position:3%
DEREK: We're really glad that
Dr. Thielen saw Molly.

00:27:25.944 --> 00:27:28.913 align:start size:81% position:19%
She took really good
care of her.

00:27:28.913 --> 00:27:31.382
So I guess, until Monday we're
just gonna relax on the weekend

00:27:31.382 --> 00:27:33.084
and just chill together.

00:27:37.922 --> 00:27:40.057 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. T: Oh, he's tiny!
KIM: I know.

00:27:40.057 --> 00:27:41.692
DR. T: (gasps) Hi, teenager.

00:27:41.692 --> 00:27:44.895
KIM: They're supposedly
15 weeks out of pouch.

00:27:44.895 --> 00:27:47.698 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: Next up,
 two furry faces are here</i>

00:27:47.698 --> 00:27:50.534 line:0%
<i> to meet Dr. T for
 the very first time.</i>

00:27:50.534 --> 00:27:51.969 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
DR. T: I have Bandit
and Boomer here,

00:27:51.969 --> 00:27:54.906 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
who are two really young,
adorable little sugar gliders.

00:27:54.906 --> 00:27:56.607 align:start size:91% position:9%
They're here just for
their first wellness exam

00:27:56.607 --> 00:27:58.375
and to talk about
getting neutered.

00:27:58.375 --> 00:28:00.978
Oh, they're darling.
So, which one's which?

00:28:00.978 --> 00:28:03.480
KIM: Bandit's the darker one
and Boomer is the lighter one.

00:28:03.480 --> 00:28:05.483
Yeah. He looks like a Bandit.

00:28:05.483 --> 00:28:06.785
DR. T: Don't you nibble.

00:28:06.785 --> 00:28:09.119 align:start size:91% position:9%
KIM: Boomer is a lot more
laidback than Bandit.

00:28:09.119 --> 00:28:11.790
Boomer will just find a place
to just hang out and chill,

00:28:11.790 --> 00:28:14.292 align:start position:0% line:0%
which is usually on my shoulder
or my daughter's shoulder.

00:28:14.292 --> 00:28:16.694 align:start size:91% position:9%
Bandit loves to run around
and check things out.

00:28:16.694 --> 00:28:18.863 align:start size:88% position:13%
I don't know if they're
brothers or not.

00:28:18.863 --> 00:28:21.165 align:start size:97% position:3%
They were rehomed to me after
the people only had 'em

00:28:21.165 --> 00:28:22.634
for, like, a week and a half.

00:28:22.634 --> 00:28:25.069
There was a lady that was
trying to rehome two babies

00:28:25.069 --> 00:28:26.637
that her husband
and her two sons

00:28:26.637 --> 00:28:28.806
had bought at a reptile show.

00:28:28.806 --> 00:28:30.240
She said they didn't
have time for 'em,

00:28:30.240 --> 00:28:33.010 align:start size:91% position:9%
so I offered to take them
and here we are.

00:28:33.010 --> 00:28:35.379 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. T: Alright, Boom,
how are you?

00:28:35.379 --> 00:28:36.481
Let's look at you, huh?

00:28:36.481 --> 00:28:38.048 align:start size:81% position:19%
KIM: So, yeah,
I wanted to come in

00:28:38.048 --> 00:28:39.416 align:start size:81% position:19%
'cause I need to get
these two fixed

00:28:39.416 --> 00:28:41.419
before I put 'em
with my other, yes.

00:28:41.419 --> 00:28:42.687 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. T: With your females?
I understand.

00:28:42.687 --> 00:28:43.988
KIM: Yes, yes.

00:28:43.988 --> 00:28:45.055
DR. T: Oh, I lost it.

00:28:45.055 --> 00:28:46.858
KIM: We don't want any babies.

00:28:46.858 --> 00:28:49.326 align:start size:91% position:9%
I don't want them to breed
with my adult females.

00:28:49.326 --> 00:28:51.662 align:start size:91% position:9%
They're already over-bred
as it is.

00:28:51.662 --> 00:28:53.865 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I just,
I don't want any babies.

00:28:53.865 --> 00:28:56.667 align:start position:0%
DR. T: This is the stethoscope.
It's okay, want to smell?

00:28:56.667 --> 00:28:58.502
I really like working
with sugar gliders.

00:28:58.502 --> 00:29:00.872
They're just adorable!

00:29:00.872 --> 00:29:03.942 align:start position:0%
They have like the biggest eyes
and they're so soft.

00:29:03.942 --> 00:29:05.510 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're just one
of the cutest animals

00:29:05.510 --> 00:29:08.246 align:start size:78% position:22%
I think that could
possibly exist.

00:29:08.246 --> 00:29:10.814 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: Boomer didn't seem
 to mind his exam.</i>

00:29:10.814 --> 00:29:13.150
<i> But Bandit is another story.</i>

00:29:13.150 --> 00:29:14.853
(screeching)

00:29:14.853 --> 00:29:16.020
DR. T: No way.

00:29:16.020 --> 00:29:17.621
Tell me about it.

00:29:17.621 --> 00:29:20.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.
(laughs)

00:29:20.758 --> 00:29:22.593
(screeching)

00:29:22.593 --> 00:29:24.595
Okay, dude, I'm sorry.

00:29:24.595 --> 00:29:25.629
Whoo!

00:29:25.629 --> 00:29:28.333
It's like a skunk.
Do you smell that?

00:29:28.333 --> 00:29:30.468 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: Male sugar gliders
 use three scent glands</i>

00:29:30.468 --> 00:29:33.838
<i> to mark territory, but if
 they're nervous or scared,</i>

00:29:33.838 --> 00:29:37.541
<i> their naturally sweet, musky
 scent can easily turn sour.</i>

00:29:37.541 --> 00:29:38.977 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. T: I know they had
scent glands;

00:29:38.977 --> 00:29:41.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just didn't expect them
to actually smell like that.

00:29:41.645 --> 00:29:43.982
Because I've pissed off
a lot of sugar gliders

00:29:43.982 --> 00:29:46.551 align:start size:91% position:9%
and I've never experienced
that smell.

00:29:46.551 --> 00:29:48.886
<i> NARRATOR: Bandit and Boomer
 passed their wellness exams</i>

00:29:48.886 --> 00:29:50.454
<i> with flying colors.</i>

00:29:50.454 --> 00:29:53.625
<i> But these little guys aren't
 ready to be neutered just yet.</i>

00:29:53.625 --> 00:29:54.725
DR. T: I would wait,

00:29:54.725 --> 00:29:57.494 align:start size:88% position:13%
just because I want them
to be an adult size.

00:29:57.494 --> 00:29:58.630
KIM: Mm-hmm, yeah.

00:29:58.630 --> 00:30:00.497 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. T: It's more because
of the anesthesia.

00:30:00.497 --> 00:30:01.966
Whenever there is
a neonate animal,

00:30:01.966 --> 00:30:04.034 align:start size:97% position:3%
you're always pretty cautious
about anesthetizing them,

00:30:04.034 --> 00:30:06.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
just because, you know,
they're not fully developed,

00:30:06.537 --> 00:30:08.238
something could go wrong.

00:30:08.238 --> 00:30:10.140
And so I always think
it's much safer to wait

00:30:10.140 --> 00:30:11.542
till the animal's
a little bit older

00:30:11.542 --> 00:30:13.878 align:start size:91% position:9%
to do elective procedures
on them.

00:30:13.878 --> 00:30:15.213 align:start size:78% position:22%
So I'll see you
in, like, a month.

00:30:15.213 --> 00:30:16.648
KIM: Okay.

00:30:18.182 --> 00:30:20.718
♪ ♪

00:30:20.718 --> 00:30:26.758
♪ ♪

00:30:26.758 --> 00:30:29.427 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Shiloh,
 a four-year-old scarlet macaw,</i>

00:30:29.427 --> 00:30:31.896 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> has been obsessively preening
 for weeks.</i>

00:30:31.896 --> 00:30:34.265 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Now that her medical test
 results are back,</i>

00:30:34.265 --> 00:30:37.501 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Dr. T immediately detects
 the reason why.</i>

00:30:37.501 --> 00:30:40.671
DR. T: Ooh, here. Here!

00:30:40.671 --> 00:30:43.107
That is all yeast.

00:30:43.107 --> 00:30:44.542
Yeah, it's all yeast.

00:30:44.542 --> 00:30:45.609
Not normal.

00:30:45.609 --> 00:30:47.010
It's that, that, that, that.

00:30:47.010 --> 00:30:50.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
All the big purple splotches
is the yeast.

00:30:50.547 --> 00:30:53.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
The skin cytology showed
that there is a lot of yeast

00:30:53.517 --> 00:30:55.786
all over Shiloh's skin.

00:30:55.786 --> 00:30:58.623
You may have a low level
of yeast on your skin,

00:30:58.623 --> 00:31:00.425 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it should be nothing
compared to what I was seeing

00:31:00.425 --> 00:31:01.726
on that microscope.

00:31:01.726 --> 00:31:04.762
I mean, it's thick
and it's everywhere,

00:31:04.762 --> 00:31:07.531 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I bet that's why the bird
is just constantly

00:31:07.531 --> 00:31:10.801 align:start size:81% position:19%
itchy, itchy, itchy,
itchy, itchy.

00:31:10.801 --> 00:31:13.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Yeast infections
 are a fungal disease</i>

00:31:13.104 --> 00:31:16.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> and can be a common problem
 for exotic birds.</i>

00:31:16.173 --> 00:31:20.211 align:start position:0%
<i> Causes may include malnutrition
 and poor hygiene.</i>

00:31:20.211 --> 00:31:23.180 align:start position:0%
DR. T: Really, the best way
for me to treat this is a bath.

00:31:23.180 --> 00:31:25.649
The purpose of the bath is
to be able to administer

00:31:25.649 --> 00:31:28.886 align:start size:88% position:13%
an anti-fungal shampoo,
to get it all over,

00:31:28.886 --> 00:31:31.322 align:start size:84% position:16%
not only her skin
but also her feathers,

00:31:31.322 --> 00:31:32.857
because if I had to guess,

00:31:32.857 --> 00:31:36.126 align:start size:91% position:9%
this yeast is pretty much
all over her body.

00:31:36.126 --> 00:31:38.362
The only tricky part with this

00:31:38.362 --> 00:31:41.799 align:start size:91% position:9%
is that we already know
Shiloh doesn't like water.

00:31:41.799 --> 00:31:44.235 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: Bathing Shiloh
 calls for backup,</i>

00:31:44.235 --> 00:31:47.705
<i> so Dr. T enlists the help
 of her vet tech, Maryanne.</i>

00:31:47.705 --> 00:31:49.841 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. T: So I was thinking,
you and I bathe her.

00:31:49.841 --> 00:31:50.908 align:start size:91% position:9%
MARYANNE: Like, it's like
a one-time thing?

00:31:50.908 --> 00:31:52.343
DR. T: Today.

00:31:52.343 --> 00:31:54.078
The only problem is,
she doesn't sedate,

00:31:54.078 --> 00:31:57.548 align:start position:0%
and I do not know if she's gonna
let us do this awake.

00:31:57.548 --> 00:32:01.152 align:start size:91% position:9%
The tricky part with this
is that yesterday

00:32:01.152 --> 00:32:05.422 align:start position:0%
when I tried to sedate her,
she really did not go to sleep.

00:32:05.422 --> 00:32:08.458 align:start size:97% position:3%
I really don't know how I'm
gonna accomplish it without...

00:32:08.458 --> 00:32:09.894
MARYANNE: She's gonna
freak out and panic.

00:32:09.894 --> 00:32:10.961
It's not gonna go well.

00:32:10.961 --> 00:32:12.363
(squawking)

00:32:17.234 --> 00:32:18.835 line:0%
(squawking)

00:32:18.835 --> 00:32:21.338 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Shiloh, the scarlet
 macaw, needs a medicated bath</i>

00:32:21.338 --> 00:32:23.741 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
<i> to treat the nasty
 fungal yeast infection</i>

00:32:23.741 --> 00:32:26.577 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> that's driving her
 to obsessively preen.</i>

00:32:26.577 --> 00:32:28.145
<i> But there's a big hitch.</i>

00:32:28.145 --> 00:32:29.947
<i> Shiloh hates baths,</i>

00:32:29.947 --> 00:32:33.584 align:start position:0%
<i> and on top of that, she doesn't
 sedate easily, either.</i>

00:32:33.584 --> 00:32:34.986
DR. T: Just like in people,

00:32:34.986 --> 00:32:37.855 align:start position:0%
different individuals and
animals have different responses

00:32:37.855 --> 00:32:40.424 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
to medications,
and in Shiloh's case,

00:32:40.424 --> 00:32:43.961 align:start position:0% line:0%
she's not really seeming to get
very sedated with my drugs.

00:32:43.961 --> 00:32:45.696
However, she's relaxed enough,

00:32:45.696 --> 00:32:47.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't want to give her
any more at this point.

00:32:47.998 --> 00:32:51.702
(squawking)

00:32:51.702 --> 00:32:54.805
Getting it underneath that wing,
getting it on all the feathers.

00:32:54.805 --> 00:32:56.774
I'm so sorry, Shiloh.

00:32:56.774 --> 00:32:58.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
Is it good?
You're okay, sweetie?

00:32:58.375 --> 00:32:59.443
(squawk)

00:32:59.443 --> 00:33:01.212 align:start size:84% position:16%
Don't know if that was
a yes or a no.

00:33:01.212 --> 00:33:04.281
It was a something.

00:33:04.281 --> 00:33:06.617
(squawk)

00:33:06.617 --> 00:33:09.420 align:start size:84% position:16%
Birds do not need soap
in their baths,

00:33:09.420 --> 00:33:10.688
they just need water baths,

00:33:10.688 --> 00:33:12.856
unless your bird has
a yeast infection.

00:33:12.856 --> 00:33:14.191
That's why we use sedation,

00:33:14.191 --> 00:33:16.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause this is very abnormal
to happen for a bird.

00:33:16.360 --> 00:33:18.429 align:start size:88% position:13%
Let's get your skin
on your feet, too, huh?

00:33:18.429 --> 00:33:19.630
Maybe it's on there.

00:33:19.630 --> 00:33:21.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
We don't know where it's at.
It's everywhere.

00:33:21.532 --> 00:33:24.769
(squawk) I know!

00:33:24.769 --> 00:33:26.237
It does look pretty cute.

00:33:26.237 --> 00:33:27.971
(squawk) I know.

00:33:27.971 --> 00:33:29.440
It looks so cute.

00:33:29.440 --> 00:33:30.941 align:start size:91% position:9%
Hopefully she'll just feel
a lot better after this

00:33:30.941 --> 00:33:32.910
because her skin
won't be as itchy.

00:33:32.910 --> 00:33:34.378
Good girl!

00:33:34.378 --> 00:33:35.646
Let's ring you out.

00:33:35.646 --> 00:33:37.448 align:start size:97% position:3%
MARYANNE: Want to do her neck?
(squawk)

00:33:37.448 --> 00:33:39.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. T: We very well may need
to continue bathing her,

00:33:39.817 --> 00:33:41.285
maybe even weekly.

00:33:41.285 --> 00:33:44.054 align:start size:97% position:3%
However, I want to do at least
this initial bath today,

00:33:44.054 --> 00:33:47.758 align:start size:97% position:3%
put her on an oral anti-fungal
and then see if that helps.

00:33:47.758 --> 00:33:48.993
<i> NARRATOR: For her comfort,</i>

00:33:48.993 --> 00:33:51.829
<i> Shiloh is transferred
 to a heated incubator.</i>

00:33:51.829 --> 00:33:54.731 align:start position:0%
DR. T: There's, like, air
that's, like, blowing the heat,

00:33:54.731 --> 00:33:57.168
so I think it's gonna
help her dry, actually,

00:33:57.168 --> 00:33:58.903
without actually
blow-drying her.

00:33:58.903 --> 00:34:00.504 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR:
 And a few hours later,</i>

00:34:00.504 --> 00:34:02.507
<i> she's ready to hit the road.</i>

00:34:02.507 --> 00:34:03.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
MARYANNE: That's it,
that's over, it's all done.

00:34:03.974 --> 00:34:07.645 align:start size:97% position:3%
REBECCA: There you go, momma.
Hello, babe.

00:34:07.645 --> 00:34:09.413
Who's cute? I love you.

00:34:09.413 --> 00:34:12.717
For the last couple of months,
Shiloh has just been miserable.

00:34:12.717 --> 00:34:15.052
I'm really looking forward to
having a happy, healthy bird,

00:34:15.052 --> 00:34:17.387 align:start size:91% position:9%
and I'm very appreciative
to Dr. Thielen.

00:34:17.387 --> 00:34:20.658 line:0%
And so, I feel like she
not only saved Shiloh,

00:34:20.658 --> 00:34:23.093 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
but she's given me
more tools to work with

00:34:23.093 --> 00:34:25.595
so that it doesn't happen again.

00:34:25.595 --> 00:34:27.164
Want to go home? We go bye-bye?

00:34:27.164 --> 00:34:28.866
(squawk)

00:34:28.866 --> 00:34:31.402
♪ ♪

00:34:31.402 --> 00:34:35.940
♪ ♪

00:34:35.940 --> 00:34:38.876 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. T: You're doing
a real good job, Molly.

00:34:38.876 --> 00:34:40.444 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: Molly,
 the Flemish giant rabbit,</i>

00:34:40.444 --> 00:34:44.515
<i> survived emergency surgery
 to reinsert her bladder,</i>

00:34:44.515 --> 00:34:48.952 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> and now she's back for
 a crucial follow-up exam.</i>

00:34:48.952 --> 00:34:50.521
DR. T: When Molly
arrived in the ER

00:34:50.521 --> 00:34:53.524 align:start size:84% position:16%
with her bladder
literally hanging out,

00:34:53.524 --> 00:34:57.061 align:start position:0%
Dr. Turner assessed her and
noticed that one of her ureters,

00:34:57.061 --> 00:34:59.396 align:start size:91% position:9%
the tube that connects
the kidney to the bladder,

00:34:59.396 --> 00:35:02.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
looked really inflamed
and potentially compromised.

00:35:02.599 --> 00:35:04.668
So now that Molly's had
some time to recover,

00:35:04.668 --> 00:35:06.170
we need to do an ultrasound

00:35:06.170 --> 00:35:10.141 align:start size:97% position:3%
to make sure there's not
gonna be any long-term damage.

00:35:10.141 --> 00:35:11.275
That's the bladder there?

00:35:11.275 --> 00:35:13.477 align:start position:0%
DR. RAMIREZ: That's the bladder.
Very small.

00:35:13.477 --> 00:35:14.879
DR. T: Yeah.

00:35:14.879 --> 00:35:16.213
You don't see any free fluid
around it, so that's good.

00:35:16.213 --> 00:35:17.281
DR. RAMIREZ: I don't.

00:35:17.281 --> 00:35:18.783 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. T: Molly's bladder
looks perfect,

00:35:18.783 --> 00:35:21.384 align:start size:88% position:13%
so now we need to
investigate the ureters.

00:35:21.384 --> 00:35:22.786
The notes from the ER commented

00:35:22.786 --> 00:35:25.823 align:start size:91% position:9%
that one of the ureters
looked pretty traumatized,

00:35:25.823 --> 00:35:27.224 align:start size:81% position:19%
so we're gonna check
both ureters,

00:35:27.224 --> 00:35:29.960 align:start size:84% position:16%
just to make sure
everything looks okay.

00:35:29.960 --> 00:35:33.230
My biggest concern here is that
if her ureter looks damaged,

00:35:33.230 --> 00:35:36.033 align:start position:0%
we very likely could be dealing
with kidney damage, too,

00:35:36.033 --> 00:35:39.002 align:start position:0%
and if that's the case,
we're looking at another surgery

00:35:39.002 --> 00:35:41.505
and possible kidney removal.

00:35:41.505 --> 00:35:43.240 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. RAMIREZ: I don't know that
we will find a ureter

00:35:43.240 --> 00:35:46.076
unless it's really huge.

00:35:46.076 --> 00:35:47.044
There we go.

00:35:47.044 --> 00:35:49.313
DR. T: There. Beautiful.

00:35:49.313 --> 00:35:51.916
Molly's ureters look great, and
now we're on to the kidneys,

00:35:51.916 --> 00:35:54.218 align:start size:88% position:13%
and hopefully they look
just as good.

00:35:54.218 --> 00:35:57.688 align:start position:0% line:0%
DR. RAMIREZ: There's the kidney.
3.5 centimeters?

00:35:57.688 --> 00:35:59.356 line:0%
DR. T: Okay.

00:35:59.356 --> 00:36:00.725 align:start position:0%
DR. RAMIREZ: Yeah, the
architecture of the right kidney

00:36:00.725 --> 00:36:02.492
looks really pretty good.

00:36:02.492 --> 00:36:04.761 align:start size:88% position:13%
Can we tilt her
a little bit towards me?

00:36:04.761 --> 00:36:06.129
JENNIFER: Mm-hmm.

00:36:06.129 --> 00:36:07.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. RAMIREZ: Yeah, so we can
find that other kidney.

00:36:07.998 --> 00:36:09.466 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. RAMIREZ: There we go.
DR. T: There.

00:36:09.466 --> 00:36:11.635 align:start position:0%
DR. RAMIREZ: It's the same.
It's the same size, okay, good.

00:36:11.635 --> 00:36:12.803
DR. T: Good, perfect!

00:36:12.803 --> 00:36:15.239
DR. RAMIREZ: I think
she got really lucky.

00:36:15.239 --> 00:36:16.240
DR. T: That's great.

00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:18.175
Good! Awesome.

00:36:18.175 --> 00:36:19.676
Molly's ultrasound looks great!

00:36:19.676 --> 00:36:21.645 align:start size:88% position:13%
The kidneys looked good,
and so at this point,

00:36:21.645 --> 00:36:24.514 align:start position:0%
I'm going to check that problem
off our list,

00:36:24.514 --> 00:36:27.518 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we're just gonna go ahead
and focus on her face.

00:36:27.518 --> 00:36:30.187 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: To solve the mystery
 behind Molly's abscess,</i>

00:36:30.187 --> 00:36:33.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Dr. T turns to skull x-rays
 for clues.</i>

00:36:36.527 --> 00:36:38.095
TONYA: Let's do one more.

00:36:38.095 --> 00:36:40.964
Pull everything back.

00:36:40.964 --> 00:36:42.332
DR. T: Oftentimes in rabbits,

00:36:42.332 --> 00:36:45.202 align:start size:91% position:9%
facial abscesses are
related to dental disease.

00:36:45.202 --> 00:36:48.305
So, I really need to get some
good imaging to try to look

00:36:48.305 --> 00:36:51.875
at Molly's teeth so we can get a
diagnosis and work on fixing it.

00:36:51.875 --> 00:36:54.144
And by going over to dentistry,

00:36:54.144 --> 00:36:55.812
I'll get the help
of Dr. Nossaman

00:36:55.812 --> 00:36:58.014
who's a board-certified dentist.

00:36:58.014 --> 00:36:59.483
If you just look at this x-ray,

00:36:59.483 --> 00:37:01.952 align:start size:91% position:9%
you can see, like,
a little bit of asymmetry,

00:37:01.952 --> 00:37:05.289
and what concerns me is
on this right lateral,

00:37:05.289 --> 00:37:07.425
these two teeth right here.

00:37:07.425 --> 00:37:09.860
I mean, I can tell you
these roots come too tall

00:37:09.860 --> 00:37:11.095
and they're a little...

00:37:11.095 --> 00:37:12.429
DR. NOSSAMAN: Deformed.

00:37:12.429 --> 00:37:14.297
DR. T: Yeah, but I'm not
convinced I need to go in

00:37:14.297 --> 00:37:15.766
and pull this rabbit's tooth.

00:37:15.766 --> 00:37:18.902
I took my normal four view
skull x-rays as I always do,

00:37:18.902 --> 00:37:21.138
and it's a little ambiguous.

00:37:21.138 --> 00:37:23.774 align:start size:91% position:9%
I was expecting the tooth
to look horrible,

00:37:23.774 --> 00:37:25.375
but it kind of doesn't.

00:37:25.375 --> 00:37:29.045 align:start position:0%
Do you think an intra-oral x-ray
on a rabbit would work?

00:37:29.045 --> 00:37:30.147
DR. NOSSAMAN: You could try.
DR. T: I don't do them often.

00:37:30.147 --> 00:37:31.582
DR. NOSSAMAN: Yes.

00:37:31.582 --> 00:37:33.717 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. T: At this point, I really
need a specialized x-ray

00:37:33.717 --> 00:37:36.887
so I can highlight just
the problematic area

00:37:36.887 --> 00:37:39.123
and not be confused by
the rest of the skull.

00:37:39.123 --> 00:37:40.725
If I take a dental x-ray,

00:37:40.725 --> 00:37:43.427 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm gonna be able to see
a much crisper, clearer image

00:37:43.427 --> 00:37:46.263 align:start size:81% position:19%
and really nail down
that diagnosis.

00:37:46.263 --> 00:37:48.065
DR. NOSSAMAN: There we go.

00:37:48.065 --> 00:37:50.734
<i> NARRATOR: And Molly's
 dental x-rays give Dr. T</i>

00:37:50.734 --> 00:37:52.669
<i> the answer she's
 been digging for.</i>

00:37:52.669 --> 00:37:55.272 align:start size:97% position:3%
DR. T: Oh, yeah!
Look at that one tooth. Right?

00:37:55.272 --> 00:37:57.574
DR. NOSSAMAN: This right here?
DR. T: Yes. Oh, my goodness!

00:37:57.574 --> 00:37:59.243
DR. NOSSAMAN: Ahh. Good job!

00:37:59.243 --> 00:38:00.844
DR. T: Taking a look
at the dental x-ray,

00:38:00.844 --> 00:38:04.148
you can very clearly see
the tooth and the root,

00:38:04.148 --> 00:38:07.418 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it's not healthy,
not normal.

00:38:07.418 --> 00:38:10.254
<i> NARRATOR: Molly's got
 not just one, but two</i>

00:38:10.254 --> 00:38:12.355
<i> extremely infected teeth.</i>

00:38:12.355 --> 00:38:14.825 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. T: But look,
I mean, that's obvious.

00:38:14.825 --> 00:38:16.827 align:start size:97% position:3%
HOLLIE: That's a huge abscess.
I saw it.

00:38:16.827 --> 00:38:18.061
DR. T: You seen it.

00:38:18.061 --> 00:38:19.396
She has these infected teeth.

00:38:19.396 --> 00:38:21.899
We have to remove them,
there's no other option.

00:38:21.899 --> 00:38:23.533
If we don't take care
of this infection,

00:38:23.533 --> 00:38:26.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
then what could potentially
happen is the infection

00:38:26.270 --> 00:38:29.940 align:start size:97% position:3%
can spread to the surrounding
teeth as well as the jaw.

00:38:29.940 --> 00:38:32.943
<i> NARRATOR: This means Molly
 has to have another surgery,</i>

00:38:32.943 --> 00:38:35.379 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> and that doesn't come
 without risks.</i>

00:38:35.379 --> 00:38:37.047 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. T: Last time Molly
was anesthetized,

00:38:37.047 --> 00:38:39.383
she died and had to be
brought back to life,

00:38:39.383 --> 00:38:43.354
so the idea of having to
re-anesthetize her again

00:38:43.354 --> 00:38:47.057
definitely scares me,
but we have no choice.

00:38:47.057 --> 00:38:48.792 align:start size:88% position:13%
Alright, can I have
the anesthesia, please?

00:38:48.792 --> 00:38:51.928 align:start size:97% position:3%
Unfortunately, the only way
for me to cure Molly's abscess

00:38:51.928 --> 00:38:53.897
is to remove the infected teeth.

00:38:53.897 --> 00:38:55.866
This poor little bunny
just has to get through

00:38:55.866 --> 00:38:58.169
one more procedure.

00:39:02.940 --> 00:39:06.210 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
DR. T: We are about to extract
two of her teeth.

00:39:06.210 --> 00:39:07.511 line:0%
Okely-dokely.

00:39:07.511 --> 00:39:09.679 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Molly,
 the Flemish giant rabbit,</i>

00:39:09.679 --> 00:39:12.182
<i> has two severely
 abscessed teeth,</i>

00:39:12.182 --> 00:39:17.221
<i> and it's up to Dr. T to get
 them out quickly and safely.</i>

00:39:17.221 --> 00:39:20.790 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. T: So, rabbits' teeth
are squared,

00:39:20.790 --> 00:39:22.226
so I have a much
different extractor

00:39:22.226 --> 00:39:25.729 align:start size:84% position:16%
than a dog or a person
would use,

00:39:25.729 --> 00:39:27.631
because I'm using
these flat surfaces

00:39:27.631 --> 00:39:30.800
to get on each little corner
of the tooth, if you will.

00:39:30.800 --> 00:39:33.704
So the key is to really
fatigue this ligament

00:39:33.704 --> 00:39:35.472 align:start size:81% position:19%
that's holding
this tooth in place,

00:39:35.472 --> 00:39:37.174 align:start size:84% position:16%
so I can get it really
nice and loose,

00:39:37.174 --> 00:39:39.810 align:start size:84% position:16%
so when I extract it,
it doesn't break.

00:39:39.810 --> 00:39:41.845 align:start size:78% position:22%
It's really, like,
in there, man.

00:39:41.845 --> 00:39:43.380
Uh.

00:39:43.380 --> 00:39:44.915
And there it is.

00:39:44.915 --> 00:39:48.084 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: One tooth out,
 one to go.</i>

00:39:48.084 --> 00:39:50.420 align:start position:0%
DR. T: I love dentistry,
it's one of my favorite things,

00:39:50.420 --> 00:39:52.088
especially rabbit dentistry.

00:39:52.088 --> 00:39:53.256
I just find it really satisfying

00:39:53.256 --> 00:39:56.060
'cause you can kind of
instantly cure them.

00:40:00.731 --> 00:40:04.601
That's the gross one.

00:40:04.601 --> 00:40:06.570 align:start size:88% position:13%
Ooh, look at the inside,
look at the inside.

00:40:06.570 --> 00:40:07.838
You see it's hollow?

00:40:07.838 --> 00:40:09.907
No, you don't appreciate it.

00:40:09.907 --> 00:40:11.442
It's hollow inside.

00:40:11.442 --> 00:40:13.010 align:start size:88% position:13%
DR. CROCKER:
I'll give him Meloxicam.

00:40:13.010 --> 00:40:15.512
DR. T: It's hollow inside
and the pus is inside.

00:40:15.512 --> 00:40:16.947
DR. CROCKER: Ooh, it's
completely eaten away.

00:40:16.947 --> 00:40:18.015
DR. T: Isn't that cool?

00:40:18.015 --> 00:40:19.182
I'm really happy to report

00:40:19.182 --> 00:40:21.552
that rabbits don't miss
their infected teeth.

00:40:21.552 --> 00:40:24.121 line:0%
They haven't been using them
anyways, 'cause they hurt,

00:40:24.121 --> 00:40:25.522 line:0%
and so just taking them out

00:40:25.522 --> 00:40:28.091 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
is one less thing
they have to worry about.

00:40:28.091 --> 00:40:31.094
<i> NARRATOR: A flush of her mouth
 and some antibiotics later,</i>

00:40:31.094 --> 00:40:34.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> it looks like Molly's on
 her way to a full recovery.</i>

00:40:34.865 --> 00:40:38.201
DR. T: Gonna put a little stitch
in her mouth and we'll be done.

00:40:38.201 --> 00:40:39.403
So, suturing inside the mouth

00:40:39.403 --> 00:40:41.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
is actually one of the most
difficult things

00:40:41.705 --> 00:40:44.408
of the whole procedure,
'cause it's really small

00:40:44.408 --> 00:40:46.243
and you have to get
these knots secured

00:40:46.243 --> 00:40:48.745 align:start size:91% position:9%
and you have to sew
in this little tiny space.

00:40:48.745 --> 00:40:52.549 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like, my fingers are small,
so I can theoretically get it,

00:40:52.549 --> 00:40:55.152
but like, a man rabbit doctor,

00:40:55.152 --> 00:40:57.888 align:start size:78% position:22%
like, I don't know
how he does it.

00:40:57.888 --> 00:41:00.590 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm gonna cut that knot
a little smaller.

00:41:00.590 --> 00:41:03.626
That was awesome. All done.

00:41:03.626 --> 00:41:05.296
Molly made it through
her dental surgery,

00:41:05.296 --> 00:41:07.197 align:start size:84% position:16%
and by removing those
infected teeth,

00:41:07.197 --> 00:41:09.399 align:start size:81% position:19%
we were able to cure
this abscess.

00:41:09.399 --> 00:41:12.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now she's a much happier,
healthy bunny.

00:41:12.235 --> 00:41:14.237 align:start position:0%
And even though we're all gonna
miss Molly at the hospital,

00:41:14.237 --> 00:41:16.506
it's fantastic that
she gets to go home

00:41:16.506 --> 00:41:18.375
to be with her loving family.

00:41:18.375 --> 00:41:21.411
Yeah. Oh, she's so cute.

00:41:21.411 --> 00:41:25.182
♪ ♪

00:41:25.182 --> 00:41:27.517
<i> NARRATOR: For every animal
 that goes out the door,</i>

00:41:27.517 --> 00:41:29.553
<i> another one comes in.</i>

00:41:29.553 --> 00:41:32.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Last time Bandit and Boomer
 were here to see Dr. T,</i>

00:41:32.856 --> 00:41:33.924
<i> they had a little fun.</i>

00:41:33.924 --> 00:41:34.924
(screeching)

00:41:34.924 --> 00:41:38.495
DR. T: No way! Tell me about it!

00:41:38.495 --> 00:41:39.997 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: But now that these
 two sugar gliders</i>

00:41:39.997 --> 00:41:41.364
<i> are a little older,</i>

00:41:41.364 --> 00:41:44.168 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> it's time to take care
 of some serious business.</i>

00:41:44.168 --> 00:41:45.835
DR. T: They are now
finally big enough

00:41:45.835 --> 00:41:48.372 align:start position:0%
that they can undergo anesthesia
and have their neuters.

00:41:48.372 --> 00:41:50.674
Tonya and Maryanne both
are prepping these guys,

00:41:50.674 --> 00:41:52.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I want a technician
to monitor

00:41:52.509 --> 00:41:54.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
each one's anesthesia
individually,

00:41:54.411 --> 00:41:56.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
so they can make sure that,
although we're doing

00:41:56.246 --> 00:41:58.748 align:start size:84% position:16%
two surgeries kind of
simultaneously,

00:41:58.748 --> 00:42:00.417
we're really safe.

00:42:00.417 --> 00:42:03.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. T: Oh, they're so cute.
Just look at them.

00:42:03.921 --> 00:42:05.789
I really want some, guys.

00:42:05.789 --> 00:42:08.158 align:start size:88% position:13%
TONYA: Sure.
You want a sugar glider?

00:42:08.158 --> 00:42:10.528
DR. T: Yeah, I want two, and
then they can stay in a pouch

00:42:10.528 --> 00:42:12.262 align:start size:91% position:9%
and I can see appointments
with them all day long

00:42:12.262 --> 00:42:14.097
and they'll be my best friends.

00:42:14.097 --> 00:42:16.500 align:start position:0%
I have to admit, they don't make
the best pet for everybody.

00:42:16.500 --> 00:42:19.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're nocturnal,
they have like a musky odor,

00:42:19.870 --> 00:42:21.972
they're really hyper
and they run around,

00:42:21.972 --> 00:42:24.941 align:start size:81% position:19%
but I just find them
so adorable.

00:42:24.941 --> 00:42:28.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, I'm gonna scrub it up
and do this thing.

00:42:28.445 --> 00:42:30.881
A sugar glider neuter is a lot
different from other neuters

00:42:30.881 --> 00:42:33.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the sense that,
because they're marsupials,

00:42:33.349 --> 00:42:35.953
their scrotum is kind of unique.

00:42:35.953 --> 00:42:38.321 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's actually above the penis
instead of below.

00:42:38.321 --> 00:42:39.689 align:start size:84% position:16%
If you have it sitting
on the gauze,

00:42:39.689 --> 00:42:41.992 align:start position:0%
I'm literally just gonna pick up
the testicle and cut it,

00:42:41.992 --> 00:42:44.128 align:start position:0%
pick up the testicle and cut it,
and that's gonna be it.

00:42:44.128 --> 00:42:46.162
Okay, so here we go.

00:42:46.162 --> 00:42:50.633 align:start size:91% position:9%
This is a sterile cautery
that we're gonna use

00:42:50.633 --> 00:42:55.239
in order to be able to not only
cut the skin and the vessels,

00:42:55.239 --> 00:42:59.542
but also cauterize everything
to make sure it doesn't bleed.

00:42:59.542 --> 00:43:02.146 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: The procedure only
 takes a hot minute.</i>

00:43:06.116 --> 00:43:08.585 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. T: And that's it.
They're neutered.

00:43:08.585 --> 00:43:09.619
Congratulations!

00:43:09.619 --> 00:43:10.621
TONYA: Yay, guys.

00:43:10.621 --> 00:43:12.122
DR. T: Woo! (laughs)

00:43:12.122 --> 00:43:16.726 align:start position:0%
<i> NARRATOR: And soon enough,
 Bandit and Boomer are back up.</i>

00:43:16.726 --> 00:43:18.762
DR. T: Hello, hi, good morning.

00:43:18.762 --> 00:43:20.931
How are you?

00:43:20.931 --> 00:43:22.666
I know.

00:43:22.666 --> 00:43:24.301
You got his little pouch?

00:43:24.301 --> 00:43:25.802
Go back in here.

00:43:25.802 --> 00:43:27.904
Okay, there you go, bye.

00:43:27.904 --> 00:43:29.239
Perfect.

00:43:29.239 --> 00:43:30.273
KIM: Hey!

00:43:30.273 --> 00:43:32.509 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. T: Hello.
They did really good.

00:43:32.509 --> 00:43:34.945 align:start size:84% position:16%
KIM: Hi, Boomer.
DELAINEY: Hey, Boomer.

00:43:34.945 --> 00:43:36.646
DR. T: Say hi, guys.

00:43:36.646 --> 00:43:38.182 align:start size:91% position:9%
PRODUCER:
How are you guys feeling?

00:43:38.182 --> 00:43:39.950 line:0%
DELAINEY: Happy.

00:43:39.950 --> 00:43:41.150 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
PRODUCER: Yeah,
why are you happy?

00:43:41.150 --> 00:43:42.352 line:0%
DELAINEY: Because they got fixed

00:43:42.352 --> 00:43:45.255 line:0%
and now they can be with
the other sugar gliders.

00:43:45.255 --> 00:43:46.523 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
KIM: So we can put them
with the female

00:43:46.523 --> 00:43:50.193 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
and not worry that
we're gonna have babies.

00:43:50.193 --> 00:43:51.194 line:0%
DELAINEY: He's peeing on me.

00:43:51.194 --> 00:43:53.796 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
DR. T: Well,
he loves you so much.

00:43:53.796 --> 00:43:55.965 line:0%
Welcome to having sugar gliders.

00:43:55.965 --> 00:43:59.169 align:start position:0% line:0%
I've been an exotic animal owner
my whole life.

00:43:59.169 --> 00:44:00.870 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
We're probably
a little bit more crazy

00:44:00.870 --> 00:44:03.474 align:start position:0% line:0%
than the average dog/cat owner,
but I love it,

00:44:03.474 --> 00:44:05.775 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
and I love people who are
just super passionate

00:44:05.775 --> 00:44:09.346 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
about their species
and want to do it right.

